WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.281
Keelwatch connects fleet records, evidence, people and work.
Independent full-stack project · real local app · synthetic data.

2
00:00:07.281 --> 00:00:15.845
Demo Manager can perform operational changes.
The API resolves the account and enforces its permissions.

3
00:00:15.845 --> 00:00:21.947
Overview highlights documentary risks and next actions.
It is not a dashboard of every business module.

4
00:00:21.947 --> 00:00:30.473
Start with a fleet record.
One vessel will connect the rest of this journey.

5
00:00:30.473 --> 00:00:36.312
Register a synthetic vessel with a unique demo registry number.
The same workspace will hold evidence, plans and maintenance.

6
00:00:36.312 --> 00:00:43.639
The confirmed record now appears in Fleet.
Open it to continue the same operational story.

7
00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:57.360
A new vessel starts with missing certificate evidence.
Compliance state is derived from recorded dates in UTC.

8
00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:05.463
Record the existing safety-equipment certificate type.
This example expires in 14 days; file attachments are disabled.

9
00:01:05.463 --> 00:01:22.200
The saved evidence changes the state to Expiring soon.
The reason and dates explain why attention is needed.

10
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:32.961
The fleet-wide risk queue can locate this vessel.
Its dates and derived state lead back to the same record.

11
00:01:32.961 --> 00:01:46.473
The bounded background check reconciles active notifications.
This demo delivery log does not send external email.

12
00:01:46.473 --> 00:02:04.323
Create a synthetic crew profile in the fleet-wide registry.
A CrewMember is not a login account or access role.

13
00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:12.142
Record dated demo safety familiarization evidence.
The ledger explains validity; it does not certify real fitness.

14
00:02:12.142 --> 00:02:17.750
The qualification is saved with its history and validity dates.
Next, connect this profile to a plan for the vessel.

15
00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:25.555
Return through Fleet to the same vessel.
Next, select the crew profile and prepare its assignment dates.

16
00:02:25.555 --> 00:02:34.033
Choose the crew profile created earlier.
The plan connects that profile to this vessel.

17
00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:40.715
The selected deck function and both dates define this plan.
Evaluate its requirements before deciding to save.

18
00:02:40.715 --> 00:02:52.371
Evaluate demo requirements across the whole planned period.
Any gaps are advisory; this does not approve boarding.

19
00:02:52.371 --> 00:03:02.577
The dated assignment plan is now attached to the vessel.
Planning is separate from actual presence on board.

20
00:03:02.577 --> 00:03:13.542
Maintenance work belongs to this same vessel.
Create an order, assign an eligible access user and follow progress.

21
00:03:13.542 --> 00:03:20.493
The responsible maintenance user is an access-account user,
not the crew profile created earlier. The target date enables planning.

22
00:03:20.493 --> 00:03:30.177
Creation is confirmed: the order is Open.
Open the record to act on saved details and inspect its history.

23
00:03:30.177 --> 00:03:39.008
Planning confirms the saved responsible user and target date.

24
00:03:39.008 --> 00:03:47.891
Start work moves the saved order into In progress.

25
00:03:47.891 --> 00:03:58.023
Closing completes this order. Its final state and history remain readable.

26
00:03:58.023 --> 00:04:05.228
Activity connects vessel, certificate, crew plan and maintenance changes.
The confirmed facts belong to the same vessel workspace.

27
00:04:05.228 --> 00:04:11.629
History identifies the shared Demo Manager account.
It does not identify the individual visitor or browser tab.

28
00:04:11.629 --> 00:04:18.558
Switch to Demo Auditor to inspect the same records.
Changing roles clears the previous account session.

29
00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:27.007
Demo Auditor inspects the same vessel and certificate evidence.
Operational write forms are absent for this read-only role.

30
00:04:27.007 --> 00:04:33.435
The same completed order remains readable with its history.
Read access and write permissions are enforced by the API.

31
00:04:33.435 --> 00:04:40.295
A direct Auditor update also returns 403 in the script check.
The vessel and its Activity remain unchanged.

32
00:04:40.295 --> 00:04:47.513
Continue with the separate Maintenance conflict/recovery video.
Explore the case, demo and source; local footage does not prove capacity.
